    docs: resolve §4.4 internal contradiction on the consecutive-failure counter's scope (#18)
    
    §4.4's prose said the counter only guards the catch-all (SEY.RUNTIME_CYCLE_FAILED),
    but SEY.RECONCILE_FAILED's own auto_action already described the same counter
    mechanism -- contradicting the "other eight codes latch immediately" claim right
    next to it. Phase 4d needed this settled before implementing the counter in
    ed-seykota. Fix: RECONCILE_FAILED keeps its own independent counter (its
    rationale already cites the 2026-09-11 venv race as the motivating incident);
    the prose in both places now says "other seven" and calls out RECONCILE_FAILED
    as the second, independently-counted exception. Also drops a stray Phase 6/7
    auto-retry clause that had leaked into RECONCILE_FAILED's auto_action ahead of
    its actual phase.
    
    Co-authored-by: bcup02 <columnbb@gmail.com>
    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

